{
  "_doc": "The Concord's hull texture designs (change hull-texture-designs, mockup 24): the Petrel frigate's detail layer and paint, built by tools/blender/hull_detail.py and baked by tools/blender/painted_bake.py --detail data/ships/concord/hull_detail.json --ship petrel_c1,... onto the Petrel's own UVs. The mesh is the game's model (tools/mockups/glb_hull_obj.py, in its export frame); the room plan (data/ships/concord/petrel_plan.json) sits 0.55 m forward of it (dz_m). The story (where the ship's rooms put its windows, sensors, vents, bay, gun and drives) is shared by every design; a design is its plating (detail), its paint (palette, plates, liveries) and how it wears. Each design names the tradition it comes from (CLAUDE.md section 1).",
